# Project rules

Follow [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) and [docs/india-first-roadmap.md](../../docs/india-first-roadmap.md). The approved India-first epic is [#4](https://github.com/RohannShetty/LifeAsUsual/issues/4).

- The inherited 34 chapters / 765 tips, source translation fidelity, mainland-China notices and legacy source-count checks apply **only to the inherited translation corpus**. They do not prohibit original Indian guides, verified adaptations or Hindi/Marathi/regional scripts.
- Preserve stable inherited IDs, anchors, progress, attribution and the pinned read-only `source` submodule. Record editorial dispositions for rewritten/retired legacy tips.
- New Indian guidance requires its own canonical record, exact primary-source locators, jurisdiction, risk, date checked and truthful review status. Do not invent state procedures, eligibility, numbers or professional approval.
- High-/critical-risk publication must fail closed without required verification and qualified human review. Existing help-route gates do not cover every legacy public route.
- Separate supported national content from explicitly unsupported state/UT overlays. Localization must independently verify safety-critical numerals and negation.
- Preserve privacy, accessibility, responsive navigation, internal links and reader progress. Plus and Minus never give advice or joke about sensitive subjects; keep the reading column free of disruptive decoration.
- Run scoped tests on the changed commit, record failures and keep epic checkboxes truthful. Do not silently merge.
